# matrix.tsv is fetched byte-for-byte from the cluster (CRLF line endings) and its
# sha256 is recorded in matrix.tsv.README as a provenance check. `-text` stops git
# from ever normalizing its line endings on any checkout, regardless of a user's
# core.autocrlf -- this repo has already been bitten once by CRLF turning a real
# drift into what looked like an empty comparison (commit ed97de0); matrix.tsv
# feeds bin/validate.py's combo lookup on every run, so its bytes must stay exactly
# what seed_matrix.py produced.
matrix.tsv -text
